<title>GERMANY: Daimler no comment on Kopper retirement.</title>
<headline>Daimler no comment on Kopper retirement.</headline>
<dateline>STUTTGART, Germany 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>German industrial group Daimler-Benz AG on Wednesday had no comment on the retirement of Deutsche Bank AG management board chairman Hilmar Kopper, who serves as supervisory board chairman at Daimler.</p>
<p>Daimler said no decision has yet been made as to whether Kopper would remain as the top supervisory board official at Daimler after he retires in May 1997.</p>
<p>Deutsche, Germany's largest commercial bank, is among the top shareholders in Daimler. The Frankfurt-based bank announced on Wednesday that Kopper would be succeeded by Rolf Breuer.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
